   "if_replanned": "letting the sim's planner re-split at a slower CPU lane moves work to zero-copy, and matching 10.95 / 11.3 then needs cpu.per_expert_ms 0.837 / 0.719 (bisection with moetier sim); an upper bound under the same assumptions",
   "cross_check": "decode-like probe windows (NVMe < 0.5 GB/s, rx < 12 GB/s) show PCIe rx 4.0-5.1 GB/s = 38-49 expert-sized reads per token at 11 tok/s, vs 26.2 zero-copy per token in the 0.25 split: the engine already sends more to the GPU than that split, so one CPU-lane number cannot carry the whole gap",
